  kind of like the speeds with the iPhone  you have to touch and then swipe up for  face idea where the Samsung you should  be able to just press well very  interesting let's try that again  no match interesting it's hard to do  both but let's do a couple separately so  that one's pretty quick but you do  notice that a delay so it's definitely  some delay but all you have to do is put  your finger down on the screen you'll  have to do two steps or anything like  that no match again if you guys bought  an s10 or sn+ let me know how you like  the fingerprint scanner and how often it  just doesn't work for you so now let's  compare to display quality the first  thing that I have to do is go into the  display settings and change the  resolution to the highest I can't really  see any difference in sharpness the  screen on the tennis max is already  really good and the Samsung one looks  really good as well so I'm on Google's  homepage both of our maxed out as far as  brightness I do have a color temperature  difference because of true tone on the  iPhone but the iPhone does look brighter  even though it's rated at 625 nits  compared to up to 1,200 on the s 10 plus  but even what is that as far as our  zebra stripes and the camera which one  looks brighter the iPhone is definitely  brighter in the camera we can see the  different brightness levels there's a  meter built into there maybe this will  get brighter if you're outside in it  senses that you need that extra  brightness now as I'm looking at these  full white screens I could definitely  see the difference in the notch in the  cutout so the iPhone has that notch that  is infamous it's quite large  whereas Samsung opted to you a little  cut out with sm+ featuring a kind of  pill box shape one I would say that the  pill shape cut out is definitely less  intrusive if you don't notice it as much  so I like this design but I do wish a  Samsung included just a single circular  cutout on the s10 plus just like it has  on 