hear  more sound from the bottom speaker than  the earpiece speaker but it definitely  is loud which is nice if you're in an  environment where there's other noise so  I mentioned that I couldn't tell the  detail difference in the icons and as  far as the brightness the iPhone was  brighter on Google's homepage but now  playing back an HDR video in youtube I  can definitely see a clear difference  the Samsung both gets darker more  contrast II while being more bright at  the same time and here looking at these  blacks the iPhone I never thought I'd  say this actually the blacks look  slightly gray compared to the Samsung  which looks pure black now if you  compare this iPhone to any of the  previous iPhones I mean it's an amazing  display but looking at him like this  the Samsung is definitely a good step  ahead of the iPhone now for our last  comparison the most important one of all  and that is the Geekbench scores of  course I'm kidding about that but I am  curious as far as the single core score  the iPhone is still much higher with  4,800 compared to 3500 but the  multi-core is very close  11500 versus 11,000 so the snapshot  processors are catching up  and that multi-core score is pretty  impressive alright guys so hopefully you  enjoyed our hands-on comparison of the  iPhone tennis max and the new s10 plus I  will be switching over to the s10 plus  for at least a week and then doing a  follow up video on what kind of  differences I saw coming from the iPhone  so if you want to check that out make  sure you have those notifications  enabled this has been max with max tech  and I'll see you in the next video

